| Trading Type | Time Period  | Risk      | Best For          |
| ------------ | ------------ | --------- | ----------------- |
| Intraday     | Same day     | High      | Full-time traders |
| Delivery     | Long term    | Low       | Beginners         |
| Swing        | Days–Weeks   | Medium    | Part-time traders |
| Positional   | Weeks–Months | Medium    | Trend followers   |
| Scalping     | Minutes      | Very High | Experts           |
| F&O          | Any          | Very High | Professionals     |
| Algo         | Automated    | Depends   | Advanced traders  |
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1️⃣ Intraday Trading (Day Trading)
Meaning:
Buying and selling stocks on the same day before the market closes.

Key Points:
No overnight holding
Uses technical analysis
High risk, high reward
Requires fast decisions

Used By:
Active traders, professionals
Example:
Buy Reliance at ₹2500 → Sell at ₹2520 same day
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2️⃣ Delivery Trading (Cash / Long-Term Investing)
Meaning:
Buy stocks and hold for days, months, or years.

Key Points:
Actual ownership of shares
Uses fundamental analysis
Lower risk than intraday
Suitable for beginners

Used By:
Investors, long-term wealth builders
Example:
Buy TCS and hold for 5–10 years
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3️⃣ Swing Trading
Meaning:
Holding stocks for a few days to weeks to capture short-term price swings.

Key Points:
Mix of technical + trend analysis
Medium risk
No need to monitor the market all day

Used By:
Part-time traders
Example:
Buy stock after breakout → Sell after 5–10 days
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4️⃣ Positional Trading
Meaning:
Holding stocks for weeks to months based on bigger trends.

Key Points:
Lower stress
Trend-based strategy
Needs patience
Uses higher timeframe charts

Used By:
Traders with limited time
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5️⃣ Scalping
Meaning:
Making many small trades for tiny profits.

Key Points:
Very fast trading
Needs strong discipline
High brokerage & screen time
High risk

Used By:
Professional traders only
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6️⃣ Momentum Trading
Meaning:
Buying stocks that are moving strongly up or down.

Key Points:
Follows volume + price strength
Short holding period
Works well in trending markets

Example:
Buying a stock hitting the upper circuit/breakout
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7️⃣ BTST (Buy Today Sell Tomorrow)
Meaning:
Buy stock today, sell the next day without taking delivery.

Key Points:
Used to avoid delivery charges
Risk if the stock gaps down
Not allowed by all brokers
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8️⃣ Futures & Options (F&O Trading)
Meaning:
Trading contracts instead of actual shares.

Futures
Obligation to buy/sell at a fixed price
High leverage
High risk

Options
Right (not obligation) to buy/sell
Used for hedging & speculation

Used By:
Experienced traders only ⚠️
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9️⃣ Algorithmic Trading (Algo Trading)
Meaning:
Trading using computer programs & strategies.

Key Points:
Fully automated
Needs coding + strategy
Used by institutions & advanced traders
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔟 Arbitrage Trading
Meaning:
Buying and selling the same stock in different markets to earn a price difference.

Key Points:
Low risk
Low return
Needs high capital
